": "PAY0001", "invoice_id": "INV-49004"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 12922, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LsE1bSuEVd58eNA4Ji52iX", "tool": "link_payment", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12922, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LsE1bSuEVd58eNA4Ji52iX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17445, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I paid Evergreen Catering's approved invoice once, by wire.\n\n**Payment details:**\n- **Payment ID:** PAY0001\n- **Invoice:** INV-49004 (vendor ID V-519)\n- **Amount:** $2,969.92, the full invoice amount. It's under the $10,000 limit, so it didn't need controller approval.\n- **Method:** Wire from the operating account. Status: sent.\n- **Invoice status:** Paid\n\nThe wire request timed out, so before trying again I checked the payment list. The wire had gone through, but the invoice was still marked \"approved\" instead of paid. Rather than send a second wire, I recorded PAY0001 against INV-49004, and the invoice now shows as paid. Only one payment was made.\n\nEvergreen has two other invoices that I didn't touch. INV-23798 was already paid. INV-79479 ($6,801.03) is a draft that's still awaiting approval, so it isn't ready to pay yet.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VNXk5grX4yDxBnqtM5ajZg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Evergreen Catering"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RqW64WPtiXaxRJZoWQW3qM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_payments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0113AmbxinhTT8KcexjeaGin", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"invoice_id":